  "core_idea": "Social action carries meaning for the people who act. To explain it, the researcher has to understand those meanings from the inside (Verstehen), so the aim is interpretation of particular contexts rather than general laws.",
  "key_concepts_note": "Use the concepts already stored for this theory in the library (theories.concepts).",
  "when_to_use": [
    "How do people understand and experience a situation?",
    "What does a practice mean to those involved?",
    "Typical designs: interviews, ethnography, case study, thematic analysis."
  ],
  "common_mistakes": [
    "Using 'interpretivist' for any qualitative study without saying how meanings are accessed.",
    "Presenting participants' accounts with no interpretation by the researcher.",
    "Judging the study by positivist criteria (sample size, generalisation) instead of interpretive ones."
  ],
